# Delivery: auto after every change

When completing **implementation** work for AsbaTechs CRM (features, fixes, UI, APIs, attendance, desktop):

**Do the full pipeline yourself. Do not ask the user each time** whether to test, build, commit, push, or redeploy — unless they explicitly said “don’t commit/push” or this is pure Q&A.

## Required order (mandatory)

1. **Playwright (or unit) checks**
   - Default: `npm run test:e2e` (prefer `https://asbatechs-crm-web.vercel.app`)
   - Targeted: `test:e2e:desktop` / `test:e2e:api` / pages UI when relevant
   - Unit: `npm --workspace apps/web test` when server logic changed
2. **Build** — `npm run build` or `npm --workspace apps/web run build` (must pass for web)
3. **Commit** — short why-message; exclude secrets / `next-env.d.ts` / `test-results/`
4. **Push** — `git push origin HEAD` so Vercel picks up `main`

Do **not** force-push, skip hooks, or amend already-pushed commits.

If tests/build/hooks fail: fix → re-run → **new** commit → push.

## Desktop (when `apps/desktop` / installer / baked URL changes)

Auto-complete employee ship path — don’t leave “you should run Desktop Release” as the only step:

1. Ensure secret expectation: `CRM_APP_URL` = `https://asbatechs-crm-web.vercel.app`
2. Trigger **Desktop Release** when possible (`gh workflow run` / guide only if no auth)
3. Wait for success, then **scan latest Setup `.exe`** for that Vercel URL
4. Only then tell the user employees can reinstall from `/download/desktop`

## User communication

- After work: brief status (done / URL / what employees must reinstall if any)
- Do **not** repeatedly ask “should I commit?” / “should I push?” / “should I redeploy?” after implementation — just do it
